<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
Many nixpkgs maintainers prefer a stable top-level attribute order in
<code>mkDerivation</code>-style expressions so updates and reviews are easier.
This query ports <code>nixpkgs-hammering</code>'s
<code>attribute-ordering</code> rule.
</p>
<p>
Only attributes in the canonical nixpkgs order are considered. Unknown
attributes are ignored, so local helper bindings can be interspersed without
constraining the order of known attributes.
</p>
<p>
Keeping <code>pname</code>, <code>version</code>, sources, dependencies, phase
controls, and <code>meta</code> in a predictable order makes package expressions
faster to scan and less error-prone to edit.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Move the reported attribute so it appears after the named predecessor and before
later canonical sections. Follow the canonical order used by
<code>nixpkgs-hammering</code>: package identity first, then sources,
dependencies, build flags, phase toggles and overrides, and finally
<code>passthru</code> and <code>meta</code>.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Problematic — <code>version</code> appears before <code>pname</code>:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  version = "1.0";
  pname = "demo";
}
</sample>
<p>Recommended — keep the canonical order:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
}
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>
<a href="https://github.com/jtojnar/nixpkgs-hammering/blob/main/explanations/attribute-ordering.md">
<code>nixpkgs-hammering</code> explanation: <code>attribute-ordering</code></a>
</li>
<li>
<a href="https://github.com/jtojnar/nixpkgs-hammering/blob/main/lib/derivation-attributes.nix">
<code>nixpkgs-hammering</code> canonical derivation attribute order list</a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
